## 📥 INSTALLATION & TESTING

### Main Installation Script

**`scripts/install.sh`** - Unified, idempotent installer

**What it does (in order):**
1. Install Xcode Command Line Tools (if needed)
2. Install Homebrew (if needed)
3. Install GitHub CLI (if needed)
4. Authenticate with GitHub (if needed)
5. Setup XDG directories
6. Install Homebrew packages (from Brewfile)
7. Backup conflicting files (first time only)
8. Stow all packages (creates symlinks)
9. Setup macOS window management (Sketchybar font, SbarLua)
10. Setup git configuration (interactive, first time)
11. Setup local files (.zshrc.local, etc.)
12. Check for 1Password CLI
13. Set default shell to zsh
14. Offer to run macOS defaults script

### Fresh Installation

```bash
# Can be curl-ed and piped to bash
curl -fsSL <url>/scripts/install.sh | bash
```

### Update Existing Installation

```bash
cd ~/git/dotfiles
git pull
./scripts/install.sh  # Idempotent - safe to rerun
```

### Manual Stow Commands

```bash
# Stow single package
stow -v --target=$HOME package-name

# Restow (after config changes)
stow -v --restow --target=$HOME package-name

# Unstow (remove symlinks)
stow -v --delete --target=$HOME package-name

# Dry run (preview changes)
stow -v --no --target=$HOME package-name
```

### Testing Changes

**Before committing:**
1. Test scripts are idempotent (run twice, check no errors)
2. Verify stow operations don't conflict: `stow -v --restow package`
3. Check for broken symlinks: `find ~ -maxdepth 2 -type l -xtype l`
4. Test shell changes: `source ~/.zshrc`
5. Verify no secrets committed: `git diff --cached`

